       Q4 stands REGISTERED AND REFUTED and is NOT asserted below. The bound is wrong rather than the code, and it is left
       standing to be struck rather than tuned to fit. **The saving MISSED the prediction; it did not disappear** — final
       population 0.880 of `none`'s, checkpoint-mean 0.929, while PEAK is 1.067, above one. So there IS an accuracy-capacity
       trade, smaller than registered and UNPRICED: nothing here says what ~12 per cent of the kernels is worth against the error.
     SCOPE: one fixture, one placement set, one r, one budget, one compression ratio. This estimates a REPEATED POLICY —
     three interventions interacting through the model — and a consolidation's effect INCLUDES its feedback into what later
     revisits target, so no contrast here separates 'sleep uses repaired evidence better' from 'sleep changes what is revisited next'.
